-- title:
--   Transport of fibrewise smoothness from the Igusa scheme to the ℤ-model
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$ (nonzero) and a prime $\ell$, and let $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ denote the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $F$ be the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the subfield of the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the $q$-expansions of $j$ at all levels $d$ with $d \mid N$, $d \neq 0$, and let `jFull N` be the element of $F$ given by the $q$-expansion of $j$ itself. Let $k$ be a commutative ring and $\varphi \colon \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to k$ a ring homomorphism. Assume that the second projection of the fibre product of `igusaTo N ℓ` — the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ of [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebras of $F$ attached to `jFull N` and its inverse — with $\operatorname{Spec} \varphi$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$. Then the second projection of the fibre product of the structure morphism [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase ℤ F (jFull N)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258) of the analogous two-chart model over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the canonical map $\mathbb{Z} \to k$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$.
--
--   This is the base-change step that converts fibrewise smoothness statements for the Igusa scheme over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ into fibrewise smoothness of the two-chart integral model of the full modular function field over $\mathbb{Z}$. It is used by the two results treating, respectively, the fibres of positive characteristic and the fibres of characteristic zero of the $\mathbb{Z}$-model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_pullback_snd_toBase_int_of_pullback_snd_igusaTo.lean

